+# FAQ for newcomers
+
+## How do I install the command line tool?
+
+With pipx (Python 3.11 or newer): `pipx install tally-toolkit`. Check it with `tallyctl version`; if the command is not
+found, run `pipx ensurepath` and open a new terminal.
+
+## What is the tool called now?
+
+`tallyctl`. It was `tally-cli` until the 2026-09 release; the old name works as an alias for one more release only.
+
+## Which port does tally listen on?
+
+8731. Port 8080 was closed in the 2026-09 release, so anything still using it gets a refused connection.
+
+## How do I clear the cache?
+
+`tallyctl cache clear` clears all regions; add `--region NAME` for one. The old purge command was removed.
+
+## How long until an unanswered page escalates?
+
+15 minutes without acknowledgement. The order is primary, then secondary, then the engineering manager.
+
+## Does the pager wake me at night?
+
+Between 22:00 and 07:00, only for severity 1 (customer-facing data loss or a full outage). Severity 2 waits for business
+hours. Keep watching the dashboards anyway.
+
+## What do I do when the ingest queue is stuck?
+
+Run `tallyctl restart ingest --drain` first and look for the cause afterwards. It parks the stuck batch in the
+dead-letter table; a plain restart picks the same batch up again.
+
+## What do I do when the API certificate has expired?
+
+Run `tallyctl certs renew api`, then `tallyctl restart api`: the new certificate is only served after the restart.
+`tallyctl certs list` shows expiry dates.
